# Intent: 2048 (id slide: swipe up, down, left or right to slide and merge the tiles, a new tile pops, over when nothing can move, the score is the merge total) and Snake (id snake: swipe or tilt the unit to steer, one cell a step, 300 ms at the start and down to 80 ms as it eats, dies on a wall or itself, the score is the food eaten) run on the unit through the grid engine, with the vertical-swipe flag of SF76 set while they run so a swipe down inside the board is the game's (only the bottom edge, the grabber and the stop word stop it). Tilts reach Snake through the games' imu path. Full quiet, the lock and updates refuse or end them as for every game; a game never moves the head.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: self.game.start slide: a swipe in each direction slides the tiles and a new 2 pops in; self.game.start snake: the snake moves by itself, a swipe or a tilt turns it, eating grows it and speeds it up, a wall ends it with a banner; neither stops on a swipe down inside the board; both end with a swipe down from the grabber at the top, a swipe down that begins on the bottom edge, and the stop word.
# Kconfig: CONFIG_MAIPAI_GAMES (existing)
# Memory cost: flash about 2.5 KB (measured: SF76 and SF77 together grew the plain image by 3,056 bytes); a running game adds about 0.3 KB (Snake) in the Grid struct in PSRAM and the one board object; the internal cost is estimated at 600 bytes as the other grid games.

